$ rig record put --id 01927-abc --kind note --project rig
exit 1
--- stdout (0 bytes)
--- stderr (408 bytes)
rig: rig record put --id 01927-abc did not say --if-version, and that reads as a CREATE.
       IfVersion 0 means create, so an omitted flag and an explicit create are the same request on the wire and rig will not guess which you meant.
       --if-version <n>  supersede version n of 01927-abc
       --if-version 0    create 01927-abc, which is how a project or a case is written, since its id is its slug
